NAME
    Number::Format::FitWidth - Pad all number(s) to the same width that will
    fit the widest number

VERSION
    This document describes version 0.002 of Number::Format::FitWidth (from
    Perl distribution Number-Format-FitWidth), released on 2026-06-26.

SYNOPSIS
     use Number::Format::FitWidth qw(format_fitwidth);

     format_fitwidth(1, 2, 10, 12);                     # => (" 1", " 2", "10", "12")
     format_fitwidth(1, 10, 100);                       # => ("  1", " 10", "100")

     # zero_prefix option
     format_fitwidth({zero_prefix=>1}, 1, 10, 100);     # => ("001", "010", "100")

     # max option
     format_fitwidth({max=>9999}, 1);                   # => ("   1")


     # TODO: decimals, negative number

     # TODO: thousands_sep option

     # TODO: decimal_point option

     # TODO: decimal_digits option

DESCRIPTION
FUNCTIONS
  format_fitwidth
    This is basically a glorified sprintf() which will determine the width
    for you. There are some conveniences (some not yet implemented) e.g.
    handling decimal numbers, negative numbers, specifying maximum and
    minimum instead of getting from the arguments, etc.

    Usage:

     @formatted = format_fitwidth( [ \%opts, ] @numbers)

    Options:

    *   max

    *   zero_prefix

        Boolean.

